{"qid": "76292501", "kind": "freshstack", "language": "python", "title": "Query existing Pinecone index without re-loading the context data", "answer": "We can generate the same docsearch object without re-loading the embeddings and adding the vectors again to the ddbb by reusing the existing Pinecone index. We can do this by calling `Pinecone.from_index(index_name)` instead of `Pinecone.from_texts([t.page_content for t in texts], embeddings, index_name=index_name)`. This will create a new `DocSearch` object that uses the existing index, without re-computing the embeddings and adding the vectors to the index. ", "valid_output": true, "insufficient_information": false, "retrieved": ["openai-cookbook/examples/How_to_build_a_tool-using_agent_with_Langchain.ipynb_0_7697", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/dingo.ipynb_0_6691", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/ecloud_vector_search.ipynb_0_7288", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/retrievers/self_query/pinecone.ipynb_0_6853"], "cited_doc_ids": ["langchain/docs/docs/integrations/retrievers/self_query/pinecone.ipynb_0_6853"], "invalid_citations": [], "repaired_citations": [["langchain/docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/pinecone.ipynb_0_6853", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/retrievers/self_query/pinecone.ipynb_0_6853"]], "degenerate_answer": false, "context_coverage": 1.0, "context_recall": 0.058823529411764705, "nuggets": ["Access the existing Pinecone index using its name.", "Use the same embeddings that were used to create the index.", "Utilize the `Pinecone.from_existing_index` method to generate the docsearch object."], "nuggets_present": null, "nugget_judge_ok": null, "citations": [{"doc_id": "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/retrievers/self_query/pinecone.ipynb_0_6853", "supported": null, "judge_supported": null, "quote": null, "quote_found": null, "judge_ok": null, "relevant_in_qrels": false, "judged_in_qrels": true}], "generation_s": 55.81725510000251, "judge_s": null, "prompt_tokens": 3