{"qid": "76517720", "kind": "freshstack", "language": "python", "title": "Langchain pandas agent unable to run pandas commands", "answer": "The issue is that the `python_repl_ast` tool is not being used correctly. The `python_repl_ast` tool is used to execute Python code in a REPL-like environment, but it is not designed to execute pandas commands directly. The `python` tool is used to execute Python commands, but it does not have access to the pandas dataframe by default. To fix this issue, you need to use the `python` tool and pass the dataframe as an argument to the `python` tool. You can do this by modifying the `Action Input` to `python df['Profit'] = df['Total'] - df['cogs']; df['Profit'].mean()`", "valid_output": true, "insufficient_information": false, "retrieved": ["langchain/docs/docs/integrations/tools/pandas.ipynb_0_6109", "langchain/templates/csv-agent/csv_agent/agent.py_0_3058", "langchain/cookbook/camel_role_playing.ipynb_23880_31125", "langchain/cookbook/camel_role_playing.ipynb_8125_15961"], "cited_doc_ids": ["langchain/docs/docs/integrations/tools/pandas.ipynb_0_6109", "langchain/templates/csv-agent/csv_agent/agent.py_0_3058"], "invalid_citations": [], "repaired_citations": [], "degenerate_answer": false, "context_coverage": 1.0, "context_recall": 0.3333333333333333, "nuggets": ["The Langchain pandas agent requires explicit instructions in the query to use the `python_repl_ast` tool.", "Appending \"using tool python_repl_ast\" to the query string allows the agent to execute pandas commands correctly."], "nuggets_present": null, "nugget_judge_ok": null, "citations": [{"doc_id": "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/tools/pandas.ipynb_0_6109", "supported": null, "judge_supported": null, "quote": null, "quote_found": null, "judge_ok": null, "relevant_in_qrels": true, "judged_in_qrels": true}, {"doc_id": "langchain/templates/csv-agent/csv_agent/agent.py_0_3058", "supported": null, "judge_supported": null, "quote": null, "quote_found": null, "judge_ok": nul