{"qid": "77410975", "kind": "freshstack", "language": "python", "title": "How to use Langchain text splitter to reduce tokens in my text", "answer": "The text splitter is designed to split a document into smaller chunks based on a specified chunk size and overlap. However, it may not be suitable for very long documents like your 300-page PDF. You can try using a different text splitter, such as CharacterTextSplitter or TokenTextSplitter, or experiment with different chunk sizes and overlaps to see if that helps. Additionally, you can try using the TikToken tokenizer to estimate the number of tokens used and adjust the chunk size accordingly.", "valid_output": true, "insufficient_information": false, "retrieved": ["langchain/docs/docs/tutorials/pdf_qa.ipynb_0_6943", "langchain/libs/langchain/langchain/chains/mapreduce.py_0_4092", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/split_by_token.ipynb_0_7093", "langchain/docs/docs/tutorials/rag.ipynb_14698_22145"], "cited_doc_ids": ["langchain/docs/docs/how_to/split_by_token.ipynb_0_7093", "langchain/docs/docs/tutorials/rag.ipynb_14698_22145"], "invalid_citations": [], "repaired_citations": [], "degenerate_answer": false, "context_coverage": 0.75, "context_recall": 0.06451612903225806, "nuggets": ["The text splitter breaks down text into chunks based on tokens and new lines, with chunk size specified by the user.", "The purpose of the text splitter is to divide documents into smaller chunks to retrieve the most relevant text pieces.", "The text splitter does not increase the amount of text that can be input into the prompt but helps fit relevant information within the token limit.", "Printing data before and after splitting can help visualize the effect of the text splitter."], "nuggets_present": null, "nugget_judge_ok": null, "citations": [{"doc_id": "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/split_by_token.ipynb_0_7093", "supported": null, "judge_supported": null, "quote": null, "quote_found": null, "judge_ok": null, "relevant_in_qrels": true, "judged_i